## Context
Once per-command help is served from doc comments (0090), assembling the full
manual is trivial: concatenate all command helps in declaration order. This
gives `erg --help --all` as a pipeable manual and a `make docs` target that
generates the static erg-manual.md for publishing.

## Actions
1. In main.go, handle `--help --all` (or `--help=all`) before the subcommand
   guard: iterate commands in declaration order, print each help text with a
   separator.
2. Add `make docs` target in Makefile:
   `tickets/erg --help --all > docs/erg-manual.md`
3. Add `docs/` to .gitignore or commit erg-manual.md — decide which.
   Recommendation: commit it so it's browsable on the forge without building.

## Test
`erg --help --all | grep -c "^# "` must equal the number of commands.
`make docs` must produce a non-empty docs/erg-manual.md.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg --help --all` prints all command help sections to stdout
- [ ] Output is pipeable: `erg --help --all | less` works
- [ ] `make docs` generates docs/erg-manual.md
- [ ] `make test` passes
